From 33aac1ea2c302c36a3226ac7cd528e5cfb1402c5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: a <a@b.c>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 23:06:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] NFC: fix device refcount leak in nfc_genl_stop_poll

nfc_genl_stop_poll() takes an nfc_get_device() reference but returns
-EINVAL without dropping it when the device is not currently polling.
nfc_targets_found() clears dev->polling as soon as a tag is detected, so
any STOP_POLL issued after a tag has been found (e.g. userspace tearing
down after a read/write) leaks one reference. The nfc_dev then never
reaches refcount 0 on unregister, so its class device and IDA index are
never released and each such controller reappears at a higher nfcN index.

Drop the reference on the early-return path.
---
 net/nfc/netlink.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/net/nfc/netlink.c b/net/nfc/netlink.c
index dbf74af..8db21c0 100644
--- a/net/nfc/netlink.c
+++ b/net/nfc/netlink.c
@@ -884,6 +884,7 @@ static int nfc_genl_stop_poll(struct sk_buff *skb, struct genl_info *info)
 
 	if (!dev->polling) {
 		device_unlock(&dev->dev);
+		nfc_put_device(dev);
 		return -EINVAL;
 	}
 
